Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to include additional tasks and run it once on localhost.

Task 2: Install dns
Description Task 2: Install the DNS packages specified by the dns_packages variable.

Task 3: Create directories
Description Task 3: Create directories for DNS data and configuration with specified modes, owners, and groups.

Task 4: Create group
Description Task 4: Create the DNS group specified by the dns_group variable.

Task 5: Create user
Description Task 5: Create the DNS user specified by the dns_owner variable, marked as a system user.

Task 6: Generate rndc key
Description Task 6: Generate an rndc key file in the specified configuration directory.

Task 7: Set permissions on rndc key file
Description Task 7: Set the ownership and permissions of the rndc key file.

Task 8: Get the hints/root file
Description Task 8: Download the root hints file and set its permissions, conditional on dns_caching_dns being true.

Task 9: Create zone file
Description Task 9: Create DNS zone files from templates, validating each zone, and notify Rndc reload.

Task 10: Add zones to configuration
Description Task 10: Generate the main DNS configuration file and notify the Restart dns handler.

Task 11: Place systemd override
Description Task 11: Create systemd override configuration files and reload systemd, conditional on using systemd.

Task 12: Start and enable dns
Description Task 12: Start and enable the DNS service, ensuring it runs at boot.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Import additional tasks
  import_tasks: assert.yml

- name: Install DNS packages
  package:
    name: "{{ dns_packages }}"
    state: present

- name: Create directories for DNS data and configuration
  file:
    path: "{{ item.path }}"
    state: directory
    mode: "{{ item.mode }}"
    owner: "{{ item.owner }}"
    group: "{{ item.group }}"
  loop:
    - { path: "{{ dns_data_dir }}", mode: "{{ dns_data_dir_mode }}", owner: "{{ dns_owner }}", group: "{{ dns_group }}" }
    - { path: "{{ dns_config_dir }}", mode: "{{ dns_config_dir_mode }}", owner: "{{ dns_owner }}", group: "{{ dns_group }}" }

- name: Create DNS group
  group:
    name: "{{ dns_group }}"
    state: present

- name: Create DNS user
  user:
    name: "{{ dns_owner }}"
    system: true
    state: present

- name: Generate rndc key file
  shell: rndc-confgen -a -c "{{ dns_config_dir }}/rndc.key" -r /dev/urandom
  args:
    creates: "{{ dns_config_dir }}/rndc.key"

- name: Set permissions on rndc key file
  file:
    path: "{{ dns_config_dir }}/rndc.key"
    owner: "{{ dns_owner }}"
    group: "{{ dns_group }}"
    mode: '0400'

- name: Get the hints/root file
  get_url:
    url: "https://www.internic.net/domain/named.root"
    dest: "{{ dns_data_dir }}/root.hints"
    mode: '0644'
  when: dns_caching_dns | bool

- name: Create zone files from templates
  template:
    src: "{{ item.template }}"
    dest: "{{ dns_data_dir }}/{{ item.zone_file }}"
  loop: "{{ dns_zones }}"
  notify: reload rndc

- name: Generate main DNS configuration file
  template:
    src: named.conf.j2
    dest: "{{ dns_config_dir }}/named.conf"
  notify: restart dns

- name: Create systemd override configuration files
  template:
    src: systemd-overrides.j2
    dest: "/etc/systemd/system/dns.service.d/override.conf"
  notify: reload systemd
  when: use_systemd | bool

- name: Start and enable DNS service
  service:
    name: dns
    state: started
    enabled: true


